From 10dfd836db8dd98a3094da09c0e1bd2739d41012 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stew675 <stew675@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:08:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip: the transport region's BASE is a CUSHION -- N compute
 chunks above the decode/verify band
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The field log (~/no-recover.md) proved the one-way door: `narrow_floor` (the always-resident
decode/verify COMPUTE band) is corrected upward by the context after the fit probe, but the transport
region sits directly above it, so a raise can only be applied while nothing holds a region block -- and on
a server a prefill precedes every drop, so it was deferred indefinitely (floor stuck at 1536, layers cut
to 2-4 slots, arena 16 112 -> 11 330 MiB, only 13 268 back on the next request).

The maintainer's fix, as specified in HANDOVER-session5 §2.1: `transport_base = narrow_floor + N x
GGML_COMPUTE_BUFFER_CHUNK_MIB` at the first carve, FIXED for the run, region at `transport_base`.  A raise
that keeps `narrow_floor <= transport_base` is applied IMMEDIATELY with no VA move; only a raise past it
keeps the deferred path (experiments/0020), which is the CORRECTNESS fallback, not the policy.  The quantum
is the COMPUTE chunk, not a magic 256/512: a raise is always a whole number of them, and the field shape
needed exactly two (1536 -> 1792 -> 2048), which is where N = 2 comes from.

It is a cushion, not a guarantee, and the handover is instrumented so the next session can tell whether it
is the right size instead of guessing: a distinct WARN when a raise EXCEEDS the headroom ("raise to X MiB
exceeds the transport_base headroom by Y MiB -> deferred"), a per-run counter of that event, and both
counters plus `transport_base=`/`headroom=` in every SLAB_STATS census (including context-exit).

  band_raise[absorbed_by_cushion=2 overrun_deferred=0]     <-- the new knobs in the exit census
  GGML_CUDA_SLAB_TRANSPORT_HEADROOM_CHUNKS=2 (default; 0 = the pre-cushion layout)

Measured.  1 GPU, GSQ-IQ3_XXS 89k prefill, 3 rotated cycles, text 43d0b1f4629e on every arm:
  prefill 2504.8 t/s (cushion) vs 2496.3 (headroom 0) -- neutral, +0.3 % inside the 2-3 % bimodal noise
  decode  37.5 vs 37.4 t/s; arena at the wide-drop 14976 vs 15232 MiB region (the 2-chunk cushion)
The field runme, three requests (645 / 71 816 / 239 tok), same build, headroom 0 vs 2:
  headroom 0 (the pre-cushion layout): arena after each drop 16 111.8 -> 15 977.7 -> 15 977.7 MiB, and the
    2048 MiB raise (the two-slot MTP verify width) reads `exceeds the transport_base headroom by 256.0 MiB ->
    deferred` TWICE and is never applied -- session 4's numbers reproduced exactly (overrun_deferred=2)
  cushion:  16 049.9 -> 15 879.7 -> 15 576.0 MiB, band 1536 -> 1792 -> 2048 with absorbed_by_cushion=2,
    overrun_deferred=0, and the last drop's difference against the control is exactly the +256 MiB band the
    decode view needs (arena_region 13 184 vs 13 440; the cushion itself costs NOTHING once the band has
    grown into it).  Prefill 2214.2 vs 2215.5 t/s on the long request.  The cost is the dead band before the
    band learns its size: 512 MiB during the first (645-token) prefill, 256 during the second.
Campaign arm text unchanged; check-shlib-symbols 16/16.
